# Nested org repos

You are editing a nested git repository under `repos/<name>/`.

## Self-contained repos (critical)

When editing **any file** under `repos/<name>/`:

- Treat that repo as **independently consumable**. Someone may clone only the GitHub org repo with no master workspace present.
- **Never** reference the master workspace, `orbicrew_master`, `orbicrew_development`, `docs/`, `docs/development/`, `AGENT_BOOTSTRAP`, `resources/`, `local/`, or sibling **local** paths (`../orbicrew-*`, `repos/...`).
- Cross-links to sibling **GitHub** org repos by URL are OK (e.g. `https://github.com/leangine/orbicrew-api`).
- Master-only context (phase plan, product docs, Stitch guides, logos under `resources/`) belongs **only** in the master repo — copy assets into the nested repo when the app needs them.

## Git & branches

- Run git commands from that service directory (`repos/<name>`).
- Do not stage nested repo files into the **master** workspace commit (master gitignores `repos/*` contents).
- Prefer the service's own README and `.gitignore`.
- Default working branch: `dev`. Long-lived: `main`, `stage`, `dev`.

## Product boundaries

- Keep channel adapters thin; put orchestration in `orbicrew-api`.
- Platform operator UI lives in `orbicrew-web` (`/admin`), not a separate admin repo unless explicitly re-scoped.
